# Outflow Canyon: the Runoff, track 2 (SPEC 3.2). Tight and walled: a
# narrow road wound between the outflow pipes, through a long pipe tunnel
# (ribbed steel underfoot), and past two exhaust vents in the narrows,
# where there is no room to go round a firing vent: wait for it. Crate
# rows on the two wider straights, a service bay lane before the line.
# Control point 0 is the start line; features on point i apply to the
# segment from point i to i+1; a segment without `open` has walls.
league runoff
width 46
# x    y    half   features
 250  140   50                     # start line, heading east
 460  130   50     crates          # top straight: three crates
 630  145   46
 725  190   44
 735  270   44
 650  305   44     pipe            # the pipe tunnel, west
 480  300   44     pipe
 370  305   44
 300  335   44
 300  415   44
 370  450   44
 560  445   44     vent:right      # the narrows east: a vent from the right
 720  440   44
 850  470   46
 890  600   46
 865  720   44
 860  835   46
 760  895   48
 610  880   48                     # bottom straight west
 520  790   44     vent:left,phase=120   # the dip: a second vent from the left
 420  790   44
 340  880   46
 220  875   46
 130  760   46     crates          # west side: three crates
 130  520   46     bay:right       # west side north: the service bay lane
 140  300   48
 170  180   50
